* ZHELP - PRIVATE HELPC VIEWER

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* ZHELP - PRIVATE HELPC VIEWER

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:ZHELP [dir:][helpname]
    SYSUTLS:ZHELP //

Private utility copy of HELPC; public HELP is the caller entry point. //
displays its version and configured defaults. Example: SYSUTLS:ZHELP
HELP:COMMANDS

The enhanced viewer supports qualified internal links and DU-aware
parent/root navigation. It reads HLP and supported compressed HZP files.
This command is not CPMHELP, whose database format differs. Keep both
viewer installations at the tested version.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
